[statement]
A package displaced by one of the resolution goes just before the walk
that places its successor, before the successor's dependencies: `ys`
takes `cmd:sh`, which the installed `bb` holds and the kept `k` needs, and
`ys` needs `y`. apk removes `bb` after `a` and `b`, and before `y`.

[repository]
P:ys
V:1
p:cmd:sh=2
D:y

P:y
V:1

P:app
V:1
D:a b ys

P:a
V:1

P:b
V:1

[installed]
P:bb
V:1
p:cmd:sh=1

P:k
V:1
D:cmd:sh

[world]
k

[request]
app

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install a 1
install b 1
remove bb 1
install y 1
install ys 1
install app 1
